// Same-length splice into target$ -- the shared implementation behind
// MID$ statement-form assignment (`MID$(target$, start[, len]) =
// value`). Not meant to be called directly: bcc transpiles that syntax
// into a call to this function and auto-adds it to the program whenever the
// syntax is used, resolved the same way any other com.bascal.stdlib
// require is, just without a `require` line for the user to write --
// nobody ever spells this function's name themselves, since the compiler
// synthesizes the call.
library midAssign

function midAssign$(target$, start%, len%, value$)
    t$ = value$
    if len(t$) > len% then
        t$ = left$(t$, len%)
    end if
    return left$(target$, start% - 1) + t$ + mid$(target$, start% + len(t$))
end function
